    "problem_statement": "NestedHyperlinkedRelatedField returns None instead of URL when request is None\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using NestedHyperlinkedRelatedField in serializers, the field returns None instead of generating the proper nested URL. This happens because the field is not properly handling the request parameter when building URLs for nested relationships.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom rest_framework import serializers\nfrom rest_framework_nested.relations import NestedHyperlinkedRelatedField\nfrom myapp.models import Parent, Child\n\nclass ChildSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):\n    url = NestedHyperlinkedRelatedField(\n        many=False,\n        read_only=True,\n        view_name='child-detail',\n        parent_lookup_kwargs={'parent_pk': 'parent__pk'}\n    )\n    \n    class Meta:\n        model = Child\n        fields = ['url', 'name']\n\nclass ParentSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):\n    children = ChildSerializer(many=True, read_only=True)\n    \n    class Meta:\n        model = Parent\n        fields = ['id', 'name', 'children']\n\n# When serializing a parent with children\nparent = Parent.objects.get(pk=1)\nserializer = ParentSerializer(parent)\nprint(serializer.data)\n# Expected: children should have proper nested URLs like '/parent/1/child/1/'\n# Actual: children 'url' field returns None\n```\n\nThe issue affects nested URL generation in serializers where the NestedHyperlinkedRelatedField should generate URLs like `/parent/1/child/1/` but instead returns None for the url field.",
