    "op": "submit",
    "status": "answered",
    "diagnosis": "The displayed get_url drops the final attribute in each parent lookup chain: parent__pk resolves to the parent object instead of its pk, so URL kwargs do not represent the required nested key. It also unconditionally calls reverse with request=None, discarding the caller request. These are visible defects; the issue description alone does not prove that request=None itself is why every observed serializer returns None. The current unsaved-object/missing-attribute branches also return None and are preserved because their intended fallback behavior is not established by the observed source.",
    "proposed_change": "Traverse all lookup components when resolving each parent key, and pass the supplied request through to reverse. Keep the current unsaved-object and missing-parent guards. The frozen patch addresses these two established defects; tests will determine whether it fully resolves the task.",
    "repair_patch": "diff --git a/rest_framework_nested/relations.py b/rest_framework_nested/relations.py\n--- a/rest_framework_nested/relations.py\n+++ b/rest_framework_nested/relations.py\n@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@\n             lookups = underscored_lookup.split('__')\n \n             try:\n-                lookup_value = reduce(getattr, [obj] + lookups[:-1])  # type: ignore[operator,arg-type]\n+                lookup_value = reduce(getattr, [obj] + lookups)  # type: ignore[operator,arg-type]\n             except AttributeError:\n                 return None\n \n@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@\n \n             kwargs.update({parent_lookup_kwarg: lookup_value})\n \n-        return self.reverse(view_name, kwargs=kwargs, request=None, format=format)\n+        return self.reverse(view_name, kwargs=kwargs, request=request, format=format)\n \n     def get_object(self, view_name: str, view_args: list[Any], view_kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> T_Model:\n         \"\"\"\n",
